156:6. **Tap targets:** **48px minimum** for everything tappable that is not a link inside a sentence: icon buttons (✕, ?, Back, zoom), buttons, chips, rows, toggles, standalone links. Enlarge the hit area, not the text. Meets Android (48dp) and iOS (44pt); WCAG 2.5.8's floor is 24px. Links inside a sentence follow WCAG 2.5.8's inline exception.  [CHANGED 2026-10-15, was 44]
162:12. **Value display:** a large status value (e.g. time remaining) is a component, not screen text: 32/40 semibold, fixed-width digits (L9). Like OTP digits, it sits outside the four-level type scale.
163:13. **Logo lockup size and place (A-07, 2026-11-02).** Every home-base screen with the "truemeds for doctors" lockup (`brand/truemeds-for-doctors.svg`, project level, §2.8) draws it **166px wide** (height follows the 220×54 artwork), **16px from the top**, and the logo→title gap stays as in §8.3 (L6). 166 is the largest width that fits Home at 360 wide with 16 to the first header icon: 360 − 2×16 − (3 × 48 + 2 × 8 − 14 for the actions' 14px overhang) − 16 = 166. Nothing else sets the lockup size.
164:14. **Small phones (Round 4, 2026-11-02).** At **360 × 640** every state of a screen is checked: nothing the doctor needs is hidden without a scroll cue (a visible edge of the next item, or a scroll area), and a pinned bar never covers the last content when the content is scrolled to its end. The check runs as a permanent guard in `ui-screens/feedback/check-locked-specs.py` (small-phone pass, every state, Round 4 item 10; `docs/layout_check.py` covers the old prototype only). Prescribe, the case page, Home, the offer and the unlock must pass it before a screen is approved.
