180:| L9 | Value display (e.g. Home time remaining): 32/40 semibold, fixed-width digits (D-47). |
195:- **One height per group** — differ by style, not size (Apple HIG). Full-width action buttons in a pinned bar, sheet or form: **56px, 18 semibold**, whatever their role. Compact inline buttons (e.g. "View Rx" in a content row): **48px, 16 semibold**.
202:- **Button icon size steps with the button size** (Apurva, 2026-11-02; replaces the D-81 F27 pair-only rule): **56px action buttons (18px label) → 20px icon; 48px compact buttons (16px label) → 16px icon.** Icons stay on the icon scale (16 / 20 / 24) — like type and spacing, each size is a step on a fixed scale, never an in-between value; the icon is one step at or just above its label (as in Carbon, Atlassian and Fluent). **Icon-only buttons** (Back, Help, notifications, Profile, close ×, viewer controls) are not labelled buttons and keep a **20px** icon. Set centrally in `components.css` by button size (`.tm-btn--lg` → 20, compact → 16, `.tm-btn--icon` → 20), overriding any size in the markup; screens never size button icons. SALT's code copy states no per-button icon size; this is a Truemeds addition (`beyond-salt.md`).
